WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.570
<v ->So I've heard some student feedback,</v>

2
00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:03.310
and you might have one question around

3
00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:04.840
improving the transfer performance

4
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.860
for your Snow Family devices.

5
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.520
So there's a list of recommendation that AWS provides

6
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.120
from the most impactful to the least impactful.

7
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.950
So the most impactful is to perform

8
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.590
multiple write operations at a time, okay,

9
00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:17.880
from multiple terminals,

10
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.960
when you transfer files to your Snow device.

11
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.140
Then you need to transfer small files in batches.

12
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.020
So if you have a lot of small files instead,

13
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.220
put them together, create a zip,

14
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.390
and then when the zip, is at least one megabyte of size,

15
00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:34.330
then upload it into the Snow Family device.

16
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.290
Don't perform any other operations

17
00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.380
on the files during the transfer.

18
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.480
Reduce the local network use.

19
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.330
Eliminate any unnecessary hops,

20
00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.360
so directly connect the Snow device to the computer.

21
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.270
And then data transfer rates using the file interface

22
00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.670
is typically between 25 megabytes

23
00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.440
to 40 megabytes per second.

24
00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.740
But if you need faster data transfer than this,

25
00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:55.610
then there is something called

26
00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.390
the Amazon S3 Adapter for Snowball,

27
00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.000
which has a data transfer rate

28
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.810
of typically 250 megabytes per second

29
00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:04.870
to 400 megabytes per second.

30
00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.520
So these recommendations together, especially the first two,

31
00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.100
and then the data, the S3 adapter for Snowball

32
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.590
is going to be the answer for that one question.

33
00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:14.423
All right.

34
00:01:14.423 --> 00:01:15.256
I hope you liked it,

35
00:01:15.256 --> 00:01:16.960
and I will see you in the next lecture.

